    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipTier` field is a derived response field on the owner, computed from existing owner data. Following the project's established pattern for derived fields (like `membershipNumber`, `displayName`, `initials`), I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getMembershipTier()` getter returning `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present (non-null, non-blank), otherwise `\"BRONZE\"`.\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipTier` property (readOnly) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it from the entity getter \u2014 the same wiring used by the other derived fields.\n\nNo new OfficeFloor steps were needed: the value is derived from fields already populated in the existing `POST /api/owners` pipeline (`CountNamesakes` sets `namesakeCount` before save) and serialized by the existing `RespondWithOwner` responder on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nTests: both new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
