    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is clean and idiomatic:\n\n- **Right unit.** The tier is derived purely from the Owner's own fields (`namesakeCount`, `email`), so a computed getter on `Owner` is the natural home \u2014 and it sits directly beside an existing `@Transient` derived getter (the `customerCode`/`registrationDate` formatter), following the established pattern in this class rather than inventing a new one.\n- **No duplication / no catch-all.** It's a single small self-contained method; nothing else in the diff replicates this logic, and the method doesn't bloat an existing one.\n- **Consistent with the rest of the codebase.** `@Transient` correctly keeps it out of persistence, it's a read-only derived property, and the OpenAPI schema entry is marked `readOnly: true` with a description that mirrors the Javadoc \u2014 the model and the API contract stay in sync.\n- The null-guards (`namesakeCount != null`, `email != null && !isBlank()`) are reasonable defensive handling for a derived accessor and keep the branching local and readable.\n\nNo structural improvements needed.",
